# play system-details ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the System Details screen proposed for slice$
# 1, inferred from origin/main (unreleased), read from a$
# simulated host, by real code where there is some (detect, the$
# header probe, accounts) and by the gallery's stand-ins$
# elsewhere, unit (b)'s to build. It only reads: no plan, no$
# y/N, no journal. Nothing on this machine changes: every$
# command and file is the fake's.$
$
# System Details hosts #########################################$
$
  Select a host$
$
   1) Debian 13$
      ext4, sudo$
   2) Ubuntu 26.04$
      ext4, sudo-rs$
   3) Alpine 3.23$
      ext4, doas, BusyBox$
   4) Proxmox VE 9$
      ZFS, root alone$
   5) ZFS degraded$
      Pool not ONLINE$
   6) One section unreadable$
      Memory$
   7) No logins$
      Nothing recorded$
   8) A console login$
      No remote host$
   9) Many users and addresses$
      14 users, 9 addresses$
  10) Treatment: sections$
      A line each, items open them$
  11) Treatment: pager$
      A line each, the rest in less$
  12) Treatment: Export says how$
      No file written$
  13) Treatment: Export writes$
      A file, as root$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-13 or q]: 6$
$
# Info: system-details/unreadable$
# Debian 13, as debian13. /proc/meminfo cannot be read.$
# origin/main's GenerateSystemStatus stops at the first$
